rns</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->Tourism alone can no longer carry Thailand’s economy, former TAT chief warns</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Former TAT governor Yuthasak Supasorn says Thailand must move beyond tourism-led growth as visitor numbers weaken, household debt remains high and manufacturing struggles.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/general/40072400" aria-label="Thai international schools hit 280 in 2026 as competition grows October 17, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="Thai international schools hit 280 in 2026 as competition grows" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">Thai international schools hit 280 in 2026 as competition grows</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->Thai international schools hit 280 in 2026 as competition grows</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Bangkok international school fees are forecast to rise about 5% in 2026/27 as new schools outpace enrolment growth across Thailand</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/general/40072395" aria-label="TMD issues fresh warning for heavy to very heavy rain across parts of Thailand on October 18–25 October 17, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="TMD issues fresh warning for heavy to very heavy rain across parts of Thailand on October 18–25" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">TMD issues fresh warning for heavy to very heavy rain across parts of Thailand on October 18–25</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->TMD issues fresh warning for heavy to very heavy rain across parts of Thailand on October 18–25</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Thailand’s South and East face heavy rain first, with risks spreading to Bangkok and other regions from October 21 as TMD warns of flash floods.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/general/40072392" aria-label="Anutin hails 191-country IMF–World Bank meetings, targets ‘exponential’ Thai growth October 17, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="Anutin hails 191-country IMF–World Bank meetings, targets ‘exponential’ Thai growth" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">Anutin hails 191-country IMF–World Bank meetings, targets ‘exponential’ Thai growth</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->Anutin hails 191-country IMF–World Bank meetings, targets ‘exponential’ Thai growth</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Anutin says business matching and cooperation agreements at the Bangkok meetings can strengthen Thailand’s credibility and create new growth.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/general/40072391" aria-label="Rayong raid finds at least 2,500 tonnes of e-waste and scrap October 17, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="Rayong raid finds at least 2,500 tonnes of e-waste and scrap" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">Rayong raid finds at least 2,500 tonnes of e-waste and scrap</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->Rayong raid finds at least 2,500 tonnes of e-waste and scrap</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Thai authorities seized waste and machinery in Rayong on October 16 as they investigated suspected illegal e-waste imports and unlicensed operations.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/general/40072389" aria-label="Anutin plays saxophone at IMF–World Bank reception, promotes Thai culture and hopes for lasting ties October 17, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="Anutin plays saxophone at IMF–World Bank reception, promotes Thai culture and hopes for lasting ties" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">Anutin plays saxophone at IMF–World Bank reception, promotes Thai culture and hopes for lasting ties</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->Anutin plays saxophone at IMF–World Bank reception, promotes Thai culture and hopes for lasting ties</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Anutin Charnvirakul highlights Thai food, culture and wellness opportunities at a Bangkok reception attended by IMF and World Bank leaders</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/world/40072388" aria-label="Brent hits US$110 a barrel on October 16 over supply fears October 17, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="Brent hits US$110 a barrel on October 16 over supply fears" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">Brent hits US$110 a barrel on October 16 over supply fears</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->Brent hits US$110 a barrel on October 16 over supply fears</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>SATURDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Brent settled at US$109.86 as Middle East tensions and Russian diesel supply concerns grew, while governments moved to release reserves</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/general/40072387" aria-label="TMD forecasts heavy rain in 3 Thai regions on October 17, with wider downpours expected on October 21–25 October 16, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="TMD forecasts heavy rain in 3 Thai regions on October 17, with wider downpours expected on October 21–25" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">TMD forecasts heavy rain in 3 Thai regions on October 17, with wider downpours expected on October 21–25</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->TMD forecasts heavy rain in 3 Thai regions on October 17, with wider downpours expected on October 21–25</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>FRIDAY, OCTOBER 16, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Heavy to very heavy rain is forecast in southern and eastern Thailand on October 18–20, with more regions at risk on October 21–25.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">The Nation Editorial Team</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/world/40072386" aria-label="JR Tokai plans S0 Shinkansen with automated operation for 2029 October 16, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="JR Tokai plans S0 Shinkansen with automated operation for 2029" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">JR Tokai plans S0 Shinkansen with automated operation for 2029</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->JR Tokai plans S0 Shinkansen with automated operation for 2029</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>FRIDAY, OCTOBER 16, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Drivers will handle departures and emergency braking; the new trains will brake sooner after quake detection and are expected to use 6% less electricity.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">Jiji Press</figcaption></div></div><div class=" card-h css-1ru389a"><a role="link" href="/news/world/40072385" aria-label="ADB president warns Asia-Pacific inflation could persist and worsen October 16, 2026" target="_self" rel="" title="ADB president warns Asia-Pacific inflation could persist and worsen" tabindex="-1" class="card-body"><div class="card-detail "><div class="text-category-header shadow-highlight"><a class="title font-poppins shadow-highlight">ADB president warns Asia-Pacific inflation could persist and worsen</a><h3 class="hidden"> <!-- -->ADB president warns Asia-Pacific inflation could persist and worsen</h3></div><div class="published-date"><small>FRIDAY, OCTOBER 16, 2026</small></div><small class="font-buenard blurb line-clamp --3">Higher borrowing costs are adding to repayment pressures on developing nations, while the bank forecasts regional growth of 5.0% in 2026.</small></div><div class="card-image"><div class="lazyload-wrapper "><div class="lazyload-placeholder"></div></div></div></a><div class="card-footer"><figcaption class="blockquote-footer">Jiji Press</figcaption></div></div><div class="css-go5j0i"><button class="font-poppins"><p>LOAD MORE</p></button></div></div><div class="sticky-sidebar"><div class="css-1uo3en1"><div class="mobile"></div><div class="desktop"><div class="ads-sticky-1 css-1mmgt6o" style="min-height:600px;filter:unset"><div id="div-gpt-ad-1774507449074-0"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="ads-sticky-overflow css-1uo3en1"><div class="mobile"></div><div class="desktop"></div></div></div><div class="footer-wrapper footer bg-footer-theme commemorate-mode css-v1sb50"><div class="container-xxl container-p-x pt-3 pb-3"><div id="section-1" class="row border-bottom border-white mb-4"><div class="d-flex justify-content-center"><div class="widget-follow css-1i6oevu"><ul class="list-unstyled d-flex justify-content-between w-100"><li class="text-white "><a tabindex="-1" target="_blank" href="https://www.facebook.com/TheNationThailand/" rel="noopener nopopopener nofollow" aria-label="social-share" class="text-white hover-zoom" title="social-share"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="curr